 OF FUN TO PLAY” – IGN, EDITOR'S CHOICE AWARD, 9 OUT OF 10 “ROLL7 HAS IMPROVED ON EVERY ASPECT OF THE OLLIOLLI FRANCHISE” – GAMESPOT, 9 OUT OF 10 “A MUST-HAVE RELEASE THAT YOU JUS"}{'symbol': 'TDY', 'date': '2022-02-08 11:17:00', 'title': 'TELEDYNE RELAYS ANNOUNCES NEW NON-LATCHING, SPDT RF RELAYS FOR BOTH THROUGH-HOLE AND SURFACE MOUNT APPLICATIONS UP TO 18 GHZ.', 'text': 'HAWTHORNE, CALIF.--(BUSINESS WIRE)--TELEDYNE RELAYS ANNOUNCES NEW FAIL-SAFE HERMETIC SPDT RF RELAYS OPERATING UP TO 18 GHZ'}{'symbol': 'TDY', 'date': '2022-02-08 09:21:00', 'title': 'CORRECTING AND REPLACING PHOTO TELEDYNE FLIR DEFENSE AWARDED $43.9 MILLION CONTRACT TO SERVICE U.S. NAVY AND COAST GUARD SENSOR SYSTEMS', 'text': 'WILSONVILLE, ORE.--(BUSINESS WIRE)--PLEASE REPLACE THE PHOTO WITH THE ACCOMPANYING CORRECTED PHOTO. THE RELEASE READS: TELEDYNE FLIR DEFENSE AWARDED $43.9 MILLION CONTRACT TO SERVICE U.S. NAVY AND COAST GUARD SENSOR SYSTEMS EFFORT WILL MAINTAIN LAND- AND SEA-BASED IMAGING SYSTEMS USED FOR INTELLIGENCE, SURVEILLANCE AND RECONNAISSANCE; BUILDS ON RECENT AWARDS WORTH $16.2 MILLION FOR OTHER SYSTEM UPGRADES TELEDYNE FLIR DEFENSE, PART OF TELEDYNE TECHNOLOGIES INCORPORATED (NYSE:TDY), ANNOUNCED THAT'}{'symbol': 'TDY', 'date': '2022-02-08 08:05:00', 'title': 'TELEDYNE FLIR DEFENSE AWARDED $43.9 MILLION CONTRACT TO SERVICE U.S. NAVY AND COAST GUARD SENSOR SYSTEMS', 'text': 'WILSONVILLE, ORE.--(BUSINESS WIRE)--TELEDYNE FLIR DEFENSE, PART OF TELEDYNE TECHNOLOGIES INCORPORATED (NYSE:TDY), ANNOUNCED THAT THE U.S. NAVAL SURFACE WARFARE CENTER HAS AWARDED THE COMPANY AN INDEFINITE DELIVERY, INDEFINITE QUANTITY (IDIQ) CONTRACT WORTH UP TO $43.9 MILLION TO SERVICE ELECTRO-OPTICAL SENSOR SYSTEMS USED FOR INTELLIGENCE, SURVEILLANCE AND RECONNAISSANCE (ISR). THE CONTRACT WILL PROVIDE REPLACEMENT PARTS AND TECHNICAL SUPPORT FOR SEVERAL LAND- AND SEA-BASED SYSTEMS USED BY THE'}{'symbol': 'TSCO', 'date': '2022-02-08 09:00:00', 'title': 'TRACTOR SUPPLY PARTNERS WITH SOFTWARE AG INTEGRATION SOLUTIONS', 'text': "RESTON, VA.--(BUSINESS WIRE)--TRACTOR SUPPLY (NASDAQ: TSCO), THE LARGEST RURAL LIFESTYLE RETAILER IN THE UNITED STATES, HAS PARTNERED WITH SOFTWARE AG (FRANKFURT MDAX: SOW) TO MANAGE CUSTOMER DEMAND AND IMPROVE SHOPPING EXPERIENCES, GIVEN THE COMPANY'S ROBUST DIGITAL GROWTH. TRACTOR SUPPLY USES SOFTWARE AG'S API AND INTEGRATION SOLUTION TO ENABLE ITS CUSTOMERS TO CONNECT EXPERIENCES ACROSS THE STORE, MOBILE AND CLICK-AND-COLLECT CHANNELS. IN ADDITION, SOFTWARE AG'S SOLUTIONS BOOSTS OPERATIONAL"}{'symbol': 'TDG', 'date': '2022-02-08 07:15:00', 'title': 'TRANSDIGM GROUP REPORTS FISCAL 2022 FIRST QUARTER RESULTS', 'text': "CLEVELAND, FEB. 8, 2022 /PRNEWSWIRE/ -- TRANSDIGM GROUP INCORPORATED (NYSE: TDG), A LEADING GLOBAL DESIGNER, PRODUCER AND SUPPLIER OF HIGHLY ENGINEERED AIRCRAFT COMPONENTS, TODAY REPORTED RESULTS FOR THE FIRST QUARTER ENDED JANUARY\xa01, 2022. FIRST QUARTER HIGHLIGHTS INCLUDE: NET SALES OF $1,194 MILLION, UP 8% FROM $1,108 MILLION IN THE PRIOR YEAR'S QUARTER; INCOME FROM CONTINUING OPERATIONS OF $163 MILLION, UP 226% FROM $50 MILLION IN THE PRIOR YEAR'S QUARTER; EARNINGS PER SHARE FROM CONTINUING OPERATIONS OF $1.96, UP FROM A LOSS PER SHARE FROM CONTINUING OPERATIONS OF $(0.42) IN THE PRIOR YEAR'S QUARTER; EBITDA AS DEFINED OF $565 MILLION, UP 19% FROM $474 MILLION IN THE PRIOR YEAR'S QUARTER; EBITDA AS DEFINED MARGIN OF 47.3%, UP 450 BASIS POINTS FROM THE PRIOR YEAR'S QUARTER; ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE OF $3.00, UP 52% FROM $1.97 IN THE PRIOR YEAR'S QUARTER; AND STRONG OPERATING CASH FLOW GENERATION OF $279 MILLION."}{'symbol': 'TFC', 'date': '2022-02-08 09:39:00', 'title': 'TRUIST INSURANCE HOLDINGS TO ACQUIRE KENSINGTON VANGUARD NATIONAL LAND SERVICES', 'text': "CHARLOTTE, N.C., FEB. 8, 2022 /PRNEWSWIRE/ --\xa0TRUIST INSURANCE HOLDINGS, INC., A SUBSIDIARY OF TRUIST FINANCIAL CORPORATION AND THE SIXTH-LARGEST INSURANCE BROKERAGE IN THE U.S., ANNOUNCED TODAY THAT IT HAS SIGNED A DEFINITIVE AGREEMENT TO ACQUIRE KENSINGTON VANGUARD